  "elevation": {
    "meta": {
      "purpose": "Platform-neutral encoding of the shadow scale, so a future React Native kit can consume the same depth system as the web. The --shadow-* CSS strings in `sections` stay the web source; this group is the same design intent expressed structurally.",
      "not_emitted_to_css": "Intentionally absent from tokens.css. The web already has --shadow-*, and emitting 25 unused custom properties onto every page would cost bytes for nothing. This group exists for a native emitter.",
      "reduction_rule": "Reference shadows sm through xl are two-layer and iOS supports one layer per view, so iOS takes the primary (larger, outer) layer and the secondary contact layer is dropped. shadow_radius is the CSS blur halved, because CSS blur is roughly twice the Gaussian radius iOS expects. Android has no per-layer control, so elevation is a single scalar tracked to the primary layer's y-offset. --shadow-inset has no React Native equivalent and degrades to nothing; do not emulate it with a border.",
      "color_note": "Every level shares the cold ink #111827 as shadow color, matching the reference. Do not warm this — the depth system was authored against the cold foreground."
    },
